content.text:
Adaptive icon generated. Good.

Need signing. We can generate a debug keystore for local debug build automatically. Gradle debug uses default debug keystore. Release requires signing config. We can add:
```
def keystorePropertiesFile = rootProject.file("keystore.properties")
def keystoreProperties = new Properties()
if (keystorePropertiesFile.exists()) { ... }
android {
  signingConfigs {
    release {
      if (keystorePropertiesFile.exists()) { ... }
    }
  }
  buildTypes {
    release {
      signingConfig keystorePropertiesFile.exists() ? signingConfigs.release : null
      ...
    }
  }
}
```
For CI, use env vars: `LIFE_KEYSTORE_PATH`, `LIFE_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD`, `LIFE_KEY_ALIAS`, `LIFE_KEY_PASSWORD`. Or generate keystore from secrets. We'll document.

Version code: `versionCode Integer.parseInt(System.getenv("VERSION_CODE") ?: "1")`, versionName env. Add to gradle.properties default maybe.

Also add `android:enableOnBackInvokedCallback="true"`? Capacitor handles back. Not necessary.

Splash: `AppTheme.NoActionBarLaunch` uses `@drawable/splash`. The generated splash images are huge 2732 square; the theme background might stretch? `android:background` on a drawable will scale to fill, potentially distorted. Better use a layer-list with solid navy and centered bitmap. But Capacitor's splash plugin shows its own splash via launchShowDuration? Actually plugin uses the launch theme until web ready. The generated drawable/splash.png is 2732x2732 and set as window background; it will be scaled to fit (not center crop), could distort. We can create a `drawable/launch_background.xml` layer-list with navy color and bitmap centered. Or use `@drawable/splash` as background; Android scales bitmap to fill. Hmm.

Capacitor Assets generated splash for drawable-port/land; Android picks orientation-specific. Still, `android:background` scales. It might look okay since square with centered content; scaling to fill portrait crops sides, but icon is centered, fine. In landscape crops top/bottom, icon still center. Good.

But Android 12 splash screen uses `windowSplashScreenBackground` etc. The `Theme.SplashScreen` parent from core-splashscreen may require `postSplashScreenTheme` and `windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon`. Currently only `android:background`; Capacitor default. It works but may show default icon. We can configure:
```
<style name="AppTheme.NoActionBarLaunch" parent="Theme.SplashScreen">
  <item name="windowSplashScreenBackground">@color/splashBackground</item>
  <item name="windowSplashScreenAnimatedIcon">@mipmap/ic_launcher_foreground</item>
  <item name="postSplashScreenTheme">@style/AppTheme.NoActionBar</item>
  <item name="android:background">@drawable/splash</item>
</style>
```
Need colors.xml. Add. This gives branded Android 12 splash. Good.

Also set `android:windowLightStatusBar` false, status bar color navy. StatusBar plugin hides anyway.

MainActivity: maybe keep screen on? Add `getWindow().addFlags(WindowManager.LayoutParams.FLAG_KEEP_SCREEN_ON)`? Not necessary but nice for a board game. Could add in MainActivity onCreate. Also immersive mode? StatusBar.hide hides status bar but navigation bar remains. Capacitor status bar plugin doesn't hide nav bar. Could set `WindowInsetsController` to hide navigation bar in immersive sticky. But then back gesture? Android gesture nav still works. For a game, immersive is nice. However hiding nav bar can complicate. Let's keep status bar hidden, nav bar visible.

Could set `android:screenOrientation="sensorLandscape"`? No, responsive.

Need to add `android:resizeableActivity="true"`? default.

Let's add signing config and version env. Also add `android:allowBackup="false"` and `android:fullBackupContent="false"`? We'll decide. The game saves locally; backup could restore progress, which is good. Play data safety says no data collected; local backup is OS-level, not developer. Keep allowBackup true maybe. But privacy policy says no data leaves device; Android backup could upload to Google Drive if enabled by user. That's OS-level. To be safe and simple, set allowBackup="false". It avoids accidental cloud backup. Let's do false.

Also set `android:usesCleartextTraffic="false"` to prevent cleartext. Capacitor local scheme is https, so fine.

Add `android:extractNativeLibs="false"`? Not needed.

Let's edit build.gradle. Need to be careful with Groovy syntax. Add at top:
```
def keystoreProperties = new Properties()
def keystorePropertiesFile = rootProject.file("keystore.properties")
if (keystorePropertiesFile.exists()) {
    keystoreProperties.load(new FileInputStream(keystorePropertiesFile))
}
def releaseStoreFile = System.getenv("LIFE_KEYSTORE_PATH") ?: keystoreProperties.getProperty("storeFile")
...
```
But `signingConfigs` with conditional values. Simpler:
```
def hasReleaseSigning = (System.getenv("LIFE_KEYSTORE_PATH") && System.getenv("LIFE_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD") && System.getenv("LIFE_KEY_ALIAS") && System.getenv("LIFE_KEY_PASSWORD")) || keystorePropertiesFile.exists()
```
Then:
```
signingConfigs {
  release {
    if (keystorePropertiesFile.exists()) {
      storeFile file(keystoreProperties['storeFile'])
      storePassword keystoreProperties['storePassword']
      keyAlias keystoreProperties['keyAlias']
      keyPassword keystoreProperties['keyPassword']
    } else {
      storeFile file(System.getenv("LIFE_KEYSTORE_PATH") ?: "release.keystore")
      storePassword System.getenv("LIFE_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD")
      keyAlias System.getenv("LIFE_KEY_ALIAS")
      keyPassword System.getenv("LIFE_KEY_PASSWORD")
    }
  }
}
```
If no signing, release build will fail. That's okay; document. But for CI, env vars set.

`versionCode`: `Integer.parseInt(System.getenv("LIFE_VERSION_CODE") ?: "1")`. `versionName`: env or "1.0.0".

Add `bundle { language { enableSplit = false } }`? Not necessary. Play Store requires AAB; language splits okay.

Add `packagingOptions`? no.

Let's edit.

